<title>PORTUGAL: EDP selloff to earn 340 bln esc - paper.</title>
<headline>EDP selloff to earn 340 bln esc - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The privatisation of a stake in state electricity company EDP-Electricidade de Portugal later this year is expected to earn some 340 billion escudos ($2.1 billion), Diario de Noticias newspaper reported.</p>
<p>It said it had learned that the global coordinators of the sale, a consortium including Banco Portugues de Investimento, Goldman Sachs and N.M. Rothschild &amp; Sons, had valued EDP at about 1,360 billion escudos.</p>
<p>The government was inclined to sell a 25 percent stake in EDP at a price around 2,200 escudos per share, the paper reported.</p>
<p>The privatisation is expected to take place in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
<p>($ = 165.5 Portugese Escudos)</p>
